    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "we're thinking of doing an RMA but it's a huge pain to swap out a core router for just a few seconds of errors. honestly it's starting to feel like we're chasing ghosts here. is there any other way to diagnose this? like, could these tiny little bursts of errors actually be caused by something else, like some weird rhythmic interference or a specific type of electrical noise?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
